; AX1001 quotes the whole CHARACTER. The lexer's error token was one
; byte long, so a character outside the identifier set that takes more
; than one byte in UTF-8 was reported by its lead byte alone: the
; message quoted a byte that is not text, the span ended in the middle
; of the character, and the JSON line carrying it was not UTF-8 - no
; strict reader could parse it (tests/fuzz/json-ax1001-partial-char,
; found by the seeded fuzzer 2026-09-27). The token covers the character
; now; the span is one column wide and the quote is the character.
;
; A `.axbad` because it is a LEXICAL error: every `.ax` in the repository
; must parse (scripts/check-tree-sitter.sh).
(:: main Int)
(fn (main) (+ 1 中))
